      en: "Sierra Negra is an active shield volcano on Isabela Island in the Galápagos Islands, Ecuador. Rising to 1,124 m, its caldera is about 10 km in diameter, making it one of the largest in the world. The volcano is known for frequent eruptions, with the most recent in 2018. Its slopes are covered by extensive lava fields from past eruptions. The area hosts unique flora and fauna, including endemic cacti and giant tortoises. Sierra Negra is a popular tourist destination; visitors can hike or ride horses around the caldera rim. The view from the crater offers a breathtaking panorama of the surrounding landscape.",
