      en: "Pululahua Crater in Ecuador is the largest inhabited volcanic crater in the world, with a diameter of about 3 km. Located 33 km north of Quito, the crater formed about 2,500 years ago from a volcanic eruption. The crater floor contains agricultural plots farmed by local residents. The area is part of the Pululahua Geobotanical Reserve, established in 1966. The crater rim offers spectacular views of the Andes. The average temperature inside the crater is 18 °C. The crater floor sits at approximately 2,800 m elevation.",
